  "disposition": "implementation_updated",
  "summary": "Connect all twelve native LBVH stages and eight stable radix passes on persistent device buffers.",
  "regressions": [
    "Ten complete programs cover empty/singleton input, duplicate keys, collapsed/flat domains, interleaved batches, multi-chunk refit, group/parent filters and overflow.",
    "Independent stable radix scratch, tree geometry/topology, frontier membership and filtered pair completeness reject matching reference/target corruption.",
    "Fixture export enumerates only declared storage buffers; retained execution outputs in a reused directory cannot become accidental ABI inputs.",
    "Ascend-specific source tests require compiler target support, because the portable package may expose the language namespace without an Ascend target."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "Native CPU oracle invokes actual cooperative radix and LBVH kernels with mutable-reference noalias disabled.",
    "Static maximum dispatches rely on the same native live-count guards as isolated stages; production indirect dispatch and capacity retry remain separate.",
    "Ascend source lowering is not vendor compilation, execution or memory-model qualification."
  ],
  "related_changes": [
    "0053-native-lbvh-stages",
    "0055-ascend-private-pair-scratch"
  ]
}
